==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|prosecutus|prōsecūtus|lang=la}}, perfect participle of {{term|prosequor|prōsequor|lang=la}}. Compare {{term|persecute|lang=en}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|prosecut|ing}}

# {{context|transitive|legal|lang=en}} To [[start]] [[civil]] or [[criminal]] [[proceeding]]s against.
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a man for trespass, or for a riot''
#* Milton
#*: To acquit themselves and '''prosecute''' their foes.
# {{context|transitive|legal|lang=en}} To [[charge]], [[try]].
# To seek to obtain by legal process.
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a right or a claim in a court of law''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[pursue]] something to the [[end]].
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a scheme, hope, or claim''
#* Shakespeare
#*: I am beloved of beauteous Hermia; / Why should not I, then, '''prosecute''' my right?

